window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-28e6b444865df898"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"_1\">更新预测与经营计划</h1> <p>更新假设，并比较基准、上行和下行计划。</p> <p>提供经营模型、最新实际数据、已批准的假设、负责人输入和情景规则，让 ChatGPT 更新预测，并用敏感度、触发点和审阅说明比较不同情景。</p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>纳入近期实际数据和已批准假设的经营计划或预测更新。</li> <li>涵盖收入、利润率、招聘和现金的基准、上行与下行情景。</li> <li>需要敏感度、触发点和明确审批事项的规划审阅。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>更新可编辑预测，保留假设控制项，并创建带公式检查的情景表和敏感度表。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>更新预测并比较情景</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 $spreadsheets 更新 [forecast or operating plan]，适用于 [business]。\n\n使用我附上的经营模型、收入驱动因素模型、人员编制计划、现金预测、最新实际数据、已批准的规划假设、负责人输入和上一版预测。保留原始模型，并明确显示假设变更。\n\n请建立基准、下行和上行情景，并列出主要收入、利润率、招聘和现金驱动因素。总结现金影响、招聘影响、触发点、关键敏感因素、风险和建议。附上敏感度表，并列出分享计划前每一项需要批准的假设。不要悄悄覆盖业务假设。\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">引言</h2> <p>预测更新应说明哪些假设发生了变化，以及这些变化如何影响计划。ChatGPT 可以更新可编辑的模型，建立可比较的情景，并总结管理层应审阅的敏感度和触发点。</p> <h2 id=\"_6\">准备规划输入</h2> <p>附上经营模型、最新实际数据、已批准的假设、负责人输入和上一版预测。还应包括规划日历和情景规则，并指出 ChatGPT 只能在获批后更新哪些假设。</p> <ol> <li>附上经营模型和相关驱动因素文件。</li> <li>补充最新实际数据、已批准的假设、负责人输入和上一版预测。</li> <li>定义基准、上行和下行情景规则，并说明哪些假设受保护。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，要求提供可编辑的预测工作簿。</li> <li>检查假设变更、公式链接、敏感度和待批准事项。</li> <li>在同一聊天中继续，一次调整一个驱动因素。</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"_7\">比较不同情景</h2> <p>好的情景规划应让差异一目了然。保留可见的基准情景，并让每个情景都能追溯到少量、明确的驱动因素变更。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare the base, downside, and upside scenarios.\n\nFor each scenario, list:\n\n- changed assumptions and their source\n- revenue, margin, hiring, and cash impact\n- the most sensitive drivers\n- trigger points that would move us into this scenario\n- risks and open assumptions\n- approvals required before sharing the plan\n\nCheck formula links and keep the prior forecast available for comparison. Do not change any additional assumptions.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">比较基准、下行和上行情景。\n\n对每个情景，列出：\n\n- 已更改的假设及其来源\n- 对收入、利润率、招聘和现金的影响\n- 最敏感的驱动因素\n- 会使我们进入该情景的触发点\n- 风险和待确认的假设\n- 分享计划前所需的批准\n\n检查公式链接，并保留此前的预测以供比较。不要额外更改任何假设。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"refresh-a-forecast-and-plan\">Refresh a forecast and plan</h1> <p>Update assumptions and compare base, upside, and downside plans.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT an operating model, latest actuals, approved assumptions, owner inputs, and scenario rules, then ask it to refresh the forecast and compare scenarios with sensitivities, trigger points, and review notes.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Operating-plan or forecast updates that incorporate recent actuals and approved assumptions.</li> <li>Base, upside, and downside scenarios covering revenue, margin, hiring, and cash.</li> <li>Planning reviews that need sensitivities, trigger points, and explicit approval items.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Refresh an editable forecast, preserve assumption controls, and build scenario and sensitivity tables with formula checks.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Refresh the forecast and scenarios</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $spreadsheets to refresh the [forecast or operating plan] for [business].\n\nUse the attached operating model, revenue-driver model, headcount plan, cash forecast, latest actuals, approved planning assumptions, owner inputs, and prior forecast. Preserve the original model and make assumption changes visible.\n\nCreate base, downside, and upside scenarios with the key revenue, margin, hiring, and cash drivers. Summarize cash impact, hiring implications, trigger points, key sensitivities, risks, and a recommendation. Include a sensitivity table and list every assumption that needs approval before the plan is shared. Do not overwrite business assumptions silently.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>A forecast refresh should show which assumptions changed and how those changes affect the plan. ChatGPT can update an editable model, build comparable scenarios, and summarize the sensitivities and trigger points leadership should review.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-planning-inputs\">Prepare the planning inputs</h2> <p>Attach the operating model, latest actuals, approved assumptions, owner inputs, and prior forecast. Include the planning calendar and scenario rules, and identify assumptions that ChatGPT may update only after approval.</p> <ol> <li>Attach the operating model and supporting driver files.</li> <li>Add the latest actuals, approved assumptions, owner inputs, and prior forecast.</li> <li>Define base, upside, and downside rules along with protected assumptions.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and request an editable forecast workbook.</li> <li>Review assumption changes, formula links, sensitivities, and approval items.</li> <li>Continue in the same chat to tune one driver at a time.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"compare-the-scenarios\">Compare the scenarios</h2> <p>Good scenario planning makes the differences easy to audit. Keep the base case visible and trace each scenario back to a small set of explicit driver changes.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare the base, downside, and upside scenarios.\n\nFor each scenario, list:\n\n- changed assumptions and their source\n- revenue, margin, hiring, and cash impact\n- the most sensitive drivers\n- trigger points that would move us into this scenario\n- risks and open assumptions\n- approvals required before sharing the plan\n\nCheck formula links and keep the prior forecast available for comparison. Do not change any additional assumptions.\n</code></pre>"};
